# Production Tools Roadmap batch pull requests

This board (`?catalog=pto`) turns the Ask CAALM assistant tool gap list (A–O) into small batch PRs instead of one mega-PR. Each **batch PR** (up to five top-level task codes) is the **implementation ticket**. Do not open one PR per task unless the user explicitly asks.

## Before you start (non-negotiable — check every time)

Sections complete in strict numeric order. **Never implement, open, or merge work for section N until every batch in section N-1 is fully merged.**

- Read `src/lib/roadmap/production-tools/pto-pr-batches.ts` for the prior section's batches. For each batch, the PR that actually completes its tasks is `productPrNumber ?? linkedPrNumber` — `mergedSetupPrNumber` is a historical marker stub and never completes anything (see `ptoTaskCodesCompletedByPr`).
- If any batch in the prior section has no such PR number set, or `gh pr view <number> --json state,mergedAt` shows it isn't merged, the prior section is **not complete**. Stop and tell the user instead of starting the next section.
- Only once every prior-section batch's completing PR is merged may you branch and implement the next section.
- Incident: PR #268 (section 15's batch-ticket marker, no real tool code) was merged as `linkedPrNumber` while section 14's real completing PR (#267) was still open — this falsely marked section 15 complete and jumped the queue. It was reverted; `pto-pr-batches.ts` now leaves section 15 without a `linkedPrNumber` until a real implementation PR lands, in order, after section 14 merges.

## Do

- Branch: `cursor/production-tools/s{nn}-b{n}-5329` (see `pto-pr-batches.ts`).
- Title: `PTO S{n} B{n} {section title} ({task range})`.
- Body: Who / What / Where / Why / When / How and **Done when** from `production-tools-catalog.ts` for **every task in the batch** (`pnpm`-free: use `buildPtoBatchPrBody`).
- Open the PR, set `linkedPrNumber`, and push for CI. **Do not merge** and **do not ask to merge** — the user inspects the PR and merges when ready (`no-auto-merge-prs.mdc`). Board tasks complete after the user merges with green checks.


## Every tool (non-negotiable)

- One `ToolDefinition` with `requiredPermissions` from the database — **no role-name bypass** (see `security-rbac.mdc`).
- Mutating tools **confirm** before writing and **audit** who/what/when/tenant on success (`audit-narrative.mdc`); never a fake success audit on a denied/failed attempt.
- Reads are **org-scoped**.
- AI document extraction stays **human-in-the-loop** (no auto-save) — `ai-document-extraction.mdc`.
- **2a rule:** wrap the existing product API. If a backend does not exist yet, ship a permission-gated honest "not available yet" response and leave the task **incomplete** until a real wrap lands.

## Never expose to the chat agent

Platform force-delete, manage-schema, and API-key management stay out of Ask CAALM (section 11 note). Do not add a second agent/workflow engine (`no-workflow-engine-sprawl.mdc`) — compose existing tools.

